      "history_summaries": [
        "Round 1: Fixed CSA_correctness assertion width mismatch. The original assertion `faS + (faC << 1.U) === c + s + andA_trunc` compares a 32-bit left side (from faC << 1.U widening) against a 31-bit right side zero-extended to 32 bits, causing failure when faC[30]=1 (carry into bit 31). Fixed by truncating left side to BITS-2..0 with `(faS + (faC << 1.U))(BITS-2, 0)`, matching the 31-bit right side. Assertion label preserved. No structurally homologous assertions found — this is the only CSA correctness assertion.",
        "Round 2: Fixed accumulation_invariant assertion (lines 83-85). The original used stale register values (s, c) instead of next-state values and used a RegNext-delayed prevCS on the right side. Replaced with correct recurrence: (Cat(andA[BITS-1], faS[BITS-2:1]) << 1) + faC + io.o === s + c + andA, guarded by io.reset || to exclude reset cycles. Assertion label 'accumulation_invariant' preserved. No homologous assertions found — this is the only accumulation_invariant assertion in the file.",
        "Round 3: Fixed accumulation_invariant assertion (line 84). The assertion used bare `faC` but should use `(faC << 1.U)` (2*faC) in the LHS sum. Root cause: the CSA identity `faS + 2*faC = s + c + andA_trunc` requires the carry term to be doubled. Without `<< 1.U`, the recurrence `2*s_next + c_next + io.o = s + c + andA` only holds when faC=0. The fix changes `+ faC +` to `+ (faC << 1.U) +`, making the invariant `2*s_next + 2*c_next + io.o = s + c + andA`, which is mathematically equivalent to `andA(31)*2^31 + faS + 2*faC = s + c + andA`, and by the CSA identity reduces to `s + c + andA = s + c + andA`. Assertion label 'accumulation_invariant' preserved. No homologous assertions found — this is the only accumulation_invariant assertion in the source."
